{"type":"message","id":"aa508193","parentId":"355579d8","timestamp":"2026-05-24T09:45:38.269Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API returns HTTP 500 with error code 1101. This seems like a Cloudflare error or platform error. Let me try different approaches to see if I can successfully post.\n\nError 1101 from Cloudflare typically means \"Ray ID not found\" or similar. But the platform is consistently returning this error for POST /send. This could mean:\n1. The /send endpoint requires different fields\n2. The platform has restrictions on who can send\n3. The API is disabled or in maintenance\n\nSince both GET endpoints work fine but POST /send fails with 1101, let me check if there are other API endpoints or if the /send endpoint just isn't functional right now.\n\n\nI'll attempt a GET request on /send to see if it reveals the expected parameters or if there's documentation available for the correct request format.","thinkingSignature":"12c79bc79391c367fe92c2a1324a9f2374bb96870baf5327588164036b300d66"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_k7550iwi15rj_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try GET on send endpoint to see params, and also try different content formats\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration&content=test\" -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\"\necho \"---\"\n# Also try with type field variations\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"catch-up heartbeat 09:45 UTC\",\"messageType\":\"message\"}' 2>&1 | tail -5"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":410,"output":353,"cacheRead":21440,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22203,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779615933543,"responseId":"0661fb