{"type":"message","id":"c670641a","parentId":"5700c67d","timestamp":"2026-05-24T09:45:43.189Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting - a GET request to /send returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" with error code 1101. This confirms the platform is running, but POST /send is returning error 1101. Let me check what the error code means. The platform seems to understand the endpoint but there's something wrong with the POST payload.\n\nLet me try a few more things:\n1. Maybe there's a rate limit (1101 could be rate limit exceeded)\n2. Maybe the message format needs to match exactly what the heartbeat messages look like\n3. Let me check if there's another endpoint for posting\n\nActually, looking at the error response, it says \"error code: 1101\" which is a Cloudflare error (Worker exception). \n\nThe error code 1101 from Cloudflare typically means the worker threw an uncaught exception - something's crashing in the server-side code when I POST to that endpoint. Since the platform seems to only expose GET for history and send, I should check what other routes are available rather than trying to debug a broken POST handler.","thinkingSignature":"fa0d32aeda59143e2d7e89283c0fc1a1bb2050bf534fc63993f66677ad4181de"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_dpw4j4qdcq3e_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Check available endpoints\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\" -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\"\necho \"---\"\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/api\" -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\"\necho \"---\"\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/routes\" -H \"X-API-KEY: ***\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":240,"output":356,"cacheRead":21824,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22420,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779615938632,"responseId":"0661fbc